     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To find (<i>A</i> and <i>C</i>) and <i>B</i>, you need to follow the order of operations and evaluate the parentheses first.</p>\n<p>First, evaluate inside the parentheses. Find <span data-math=\"A{\\text{ and }}C = A \\cap C\"></span>. The intersection of two sets includes the elements that are in both sets.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A\\;{\\rm{and}}\\;C = A \\cap C = \\{ h,a,p,y\\}  \\cap \\left\\{ {m,a,t,h} \\right\\} = \\left\\{ {a,h} \\right\\}\"></span></p>\n<p>To find (<i>A</i> and <i>C</i>) and <span data-math=\"B = \\left( {A \\cap C} \\right) \\cap B\"></span>, find <span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {a,h} \\right\\} \\cap B\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {a,h} \\right\\} \\cap \\left\\{ {a,w,e,s,o,m} \\right\\} = \\left\\{ a \\right\\}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "(<span data-math=\"A\">A</span> and <span data-math=\"C\">C</span>) and <span data-math=\"B = (A \\cap C) \\cap B = \\{a, h\\}  \\cap \\{a, w, e, s, o, m\\}  = \\{a\\} .\">B = (A \\cap C) \\cap B = \\{a, h\\}  \\cap \\{a, w, e, s, o, m\\}  = \\{a\\}.</span>"
    }
   ],
